n 1 satisfy sqrt(2)=a/b.","step_ids":[],"tool_ids":[]},{"basis":"derivation","basis_reference":"Derived by squaring the equality in the temporary assumption.","citations":[],"critical":true,"depends_on":["rationality-assumption"],"discharged_by_step_ids":[],"id":"square-equation-claim","kind":"deduction","scope_step_ids":[],"statement":"Under the temporary assumption, a^2=2b^2.","step_ids":["square-equation"],"tool_ids":[]},{"basis":"derivation","basis_reference":"Derived using the elementary fact proved in step a-even: an odd integer has an odd square.","citations":[],"critical":true,"depends_on":["square-equation-claim"],"discharged_by_step_ids":[],"id":"a-even-claim","kind":"deduction","scope_step_ids":[],"statement":"Under the temporary assumption, a is even.","step_ids":["a-even"],"tool_ids":[]},{"basis":"derivation","basis_reference":"Substitution of a=2c into a^2=2b^2, followed by the same odd-square argument.","citations":[],"critical":true,"depends_on":["a-even-claim","square-equation-claim"],"discharged_by_step_ids":[],"id":"b-even-claim","kind":"deduction","scope_step_ids":[],"statement":"Under the temporary assumption, b is even.","step_ids":["b-even"],"tool_ids":[]},{"basis":"derivation","basis_reference":"The contradiction discharges the temporary rationality assumption.","citations":[],"critical":true,"depends_on":["rationality-assumption","a-even-claim","b-even-claim"],"discharged_by_step_ids":[],"id":"irrationality-conclusion","kind":"deduction","scope_step_ids":[],"statement":"No lowest-terms integer representation sqrt(2)=a/b exists; therefore sqrt(2) is irrational.","step_ids":["lowest-terms-conflict"],"tool_ids":[]}],"open_questions":[],"proof_steps":[{"citations":[],"depends_on":[],"id":"square-equation","justification":"From sqrt(2)=a/b with b nonzero, square both sides and multiply by b^2.","statement":"a^2=2b^2."},{"citations":[],"depends_on":["square-equation"],"id":"a-even","justification":"The equation makes a^2 even. If a were odd, a=2k+